From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: qcom-ipq9574: keep MPPE SGMII in-band framing

The IPQ53xx MPPE vendor stack drives link state from the external PHY but
leaves the UNIPHY SGMII channel in Qualcomm/Atheros in-band framing
mode. The working vendor state keeps PCS_MII_FORCE_MODE clear while using
the PHY link event to update clocks and pulse the channel adapter reset.

Phylink's out-of-band mode normally sets PCS_MII_FORCE_MODE, changing the
working MPPE PCS control value from 0x844 to 0x84c. Keep force mode clear
for MPPE SGMII while retaining PHY-driven phylink state.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -565,7 +565,8 @@ static int ipq_pcs_config_sgmii(struct ipq_pcs *qpcs,
 	}
 
 	/* Set AN mode or force mode */
-	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED)
+	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED ||
+	    (qpcs->mppe && interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII))
 		return regmap_clear_bits(qpcs->regmap,
 					 PCS_MII_CTRL(index), PCS_MII_FORCE_MODE);
 	else
